"""The agent slice: rooms a person is granted, their conversations and allowance, and an app-started job's watch.

A room is entered with its own `room-<id>` entitlement, known only once the
path is, so it is a dependency reading the path (`entered`), marked as the
module gate it is for the route walk. A conversation route reaches the room
through the conversation: one answer for another person's and for none,
then the room's own gate, so a revoked grant closes a person's old
conversations too. A shared answer is read through the room it was asked in,
behind that room's own gate, so whoever may not enter the room is refused as
they would be at the room itself.

The job routes take `agent-<persona>` the same way, AND `CurrentWorkspace`:
a job belongs to a workspace and a persona, and `jobs.authorize()` checks
both (`docs/design/agent-jobs.md`). Starting a job is not a route; a person
watches, messages and stops one the app started.
"""

